cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use erpax, cite it by its content-addressed release DOI."
title: "erpax — a zero-entropy, content-addressed ERP corpus"
abstract: >-
  erpax is an ERP corpus in which every folder under src/ is one irreducible atom
  told three ways (form · code · proof), wired through a single content-uuid.
  Its law is zero entropy ⇒ infinite tamper-cost: a claim is enforced by a gate
  that blocks its violation, never by prose that asks for compliance.
type: software
authors:
